00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.380
To access your Microsoft Office
programs on a Mac, there are

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:05.670
three ways you can do this.

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:10.639
First way is you can select the Finder.

00:00:12.069 --> 00:00:16.370
And from there select Applications,
and then you can scroll down

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:18.260
to find the relevant program.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.689
So Word, PowerPoint orExcel.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:28.430
Alternatively, you can do your Launchpad
and on the Launchpad screen, you can then

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:34.440
navigate to where the program icons are,
which is Excel, PowerPoint, and Word.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:44.699
And finally, you can attach the
shortcuts to the programs on your

00:00:44.699 --> 00:00:46.950
tool bar at the bottom of the screen.

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:51.569
As you can see, I've placed Word,
Excel and PowerPoint on this bar

00:00:51.629 --> 00:00:56.400
for easy access, which will then
automatically launch the programs.

